<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galeazzo II Visconti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1320–1378</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galeazzo II Visconti was co-ruler of the Lordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> from 1354 with his brother Bernabò, governing its western half. In 1359 he took Pavia after a long siege, made it his residence, built its great castle and in 1361 founded its university. He married his children into the French and English royal families and was the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gian-galeazzo-visconti">Gian Galeazzo Visconti</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/galeazzo-ii-visconti.jpg" alt="Galeazzo II Visconti" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Visconti,_Galeazzo_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
